Aerie-Purpose: Judge the connections the browser opens on its own (preconnect) and the names it looks up on its own (DNS prefetch) with the same request policy as URL requests, so speculative connections to an unlisted host do not leave the machine.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: services/network/network_context.cc (NetworkContext::PreconnectSockets, NetworkContext::ResolveHost)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #257, review round 1. Both calls are made by the browser process on its
own NetworkContext, so they are judged as browser traffic. A preconnect has a
traffic annotation: with a usable one it is decided like a request; with none
(navigation and network hints preconnects pass none) the host decides, and only
a host with a row in docs/network-endpoints.md passes. A lookup has no
annotation and is judged by host. A refused lookup answers the client with
ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ADMINISTRATOR and a refused preconnect does nothing.

Limits: a renderer's own host resolver (mojom::HostResolver), the DNS client's
sockets, and QUIC alternative services are not hooked. See
docs/network-endpoints.md, "Limits".

--- a/services/network/network_context.cc
+++ b/services/network/network_context.cc
@@ -116,6 +116,7 @@
 #include "net/url_request/url_request.h"
 #include "net/url_request/url_request_context.h"
 #include "net/url_request/url_request_context_builder.h"
+#include "services/network/aerie/request_policy.h"
 #include "services/network/brokered_client_socket_factory.h"
 #include "services/network/connection_change_observer.h"
 #include "services/network/cookie_manager.h"
@@ -2226,6 +2227,26 @@
                                        host->get_host_port_pair().port())
                        .GetURL()
                  : host->get_scheme_host_port().GetURL();
+  // Aerie (#257): a name lookup the browser asks for (DNS prefetch) is
+  // judged by host, as browser traffic. A refusal answers the client at once.
+  {
+    aerie_network::RequestFacts facts;
+    facts.origin = aerie_network::RequestOrigin::kBrowserProcess;
+    facts.url = url;
+    const aerie_network::Verdict verdict =
+        aerie_network::DecideConnection(facts);
+    if (aerie_network::IsRefusal(verdict)) {
+      aerie_network::RecordRefusal(verdict, url);
+      mojo::Remote<mojom::ResolveHostClient> refused_client(
+          std::move(response_client));
+      refused_client->OnComplete(
+          net::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ADMINISTRATOR,
+          net::ResolveErrorInfo(net::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ADMINISTRATOR),
+          /*resolved_addresses=*/{}, /*alternative_endpoints=*/{});
+      return;
+    }
+  }
+
   bool is_network_disallowed_for_restrictions_id =
       (optional_parameters &&
        optional_parameters->network_restrictions_id.has_value() &&
@@ -2550,6 +2571,21 @@
     const std::optional<net::ConnectionKeepAliveConfig>& keepalive_config,
     mojo::PendingRemote<mojom::ConnectionChangeObserverClient>
         connection_change_observer_client) {
+  // Aerie (#257): the browser asks for this connection on its own, so the
